\": \"She could analyze data like a boss—her ‘coxcomb’ charts made disease trends look like a fan’s feathers (and saved lives)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Beyoncé (aka Sasha Fierce’s Mom-in-Training, Queen Bey, or just ‘the woman who makes us question our life choices’)\",\n      \"tone\": \"the mom who turns family photos into art installations and lemonade stands into Grammy-winning albums\",\n      \"achievement\": \"Singer, dancer, feminist icon, and the only person who can make ‘Single Ladies’ sound like a threat\",\n      \"mom_cred\": \"Raised by a single mom (Tina Knowles) who dressed her in *strawberry shorts* like a tiny diva—literally\",\n      \"fun_fact\": \"Her first word was allegedly ‘daddy’… but rumor has it she was actually screaming ‘autotune’ at 6 months old\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Hypatia of Alexandria (aka The Ancient World’s ‘Cool Mom Who Also Ripped Apart Patriarchy’)\",\n      \"tone\": \"the philosopher who taught math, science, and *side-eye* so hard it literally got her murdered in 415 AD\",\n      \"achievement\": \"Neoplatonist scholar, math genius, and the woman who made ‘don’t mess with her’ a full-time job\",\n      \"mom_cred\": \"Her father, Theon, was her teacher—but when he died? She took over his school like ‘hold my wine.’ (Metaphorically. Wine wasn’t a thing in 4th-century Alexandria.)\",\n      \"fun_fact\": \"She was torn apart by a mob for ‘corrupting the youth’—yet her students still worshipped her like she was the original ‘cool aunt’\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```", "logprobs": [{"token": "```", "logprob": -0.0013579442165791988}, {"token": "json", "logprob": -0.0002809368306770921}, {"token": "\n", "logprob": -0.010706129483878613}, {"token": "{\n", "logprob": -0.002379445359110832}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -0.006188634783029556}, {"token": " \"", "logprob": -0.003365093609318137}, {"token": "f", "logprob": -0.44240039587020874}, {"token": "amous", "logprob": -0.14600977301597595}, {"token": "_m", "logprob"